# Measured on winoracle (Windows 10.0.26200, "Microsoft Basic Render Driver",
# feature level 11_0) on 2026-09-22.
#
# VERDICTS
#
# 11.14  Vitreo was UNDER-PERMISSIVE. Windows accepts packed depth+stencil
#        staging: D24_UNORM_S8_UINT reports RowPitch 64 on a 16-wide surface,
#        i.e. 4 bytes per pixel packed, and D32_FLOAT_S8X24_UINT reports 128,
#        i.e. 8. That is the layout this file's refusal was reasoning about --
#        the reasoning was right and the conclusion was wrong. Depth-only and
#        block-compressed pitches match Vitreo exactly.
# 11.11  Vitreo MATCHES on every line: GetType 2, the 1D GetDesc field order,
#        and E_INVALIDARG for both a 2D view of a 1D resource and a 1D view of
#        a 2D one.
# 11.6   Vitreo MATCHES on APPEND, COUNTER, APPEND|COUNTER, a format on a
#        structured view, an undefined flag bit, and APPEND on a typed buffer.
#        One divergence: RAW on a structured buffer is E_INVALIDARG here and
#        E_NOTIMPL in Vitreo, because Vitreo checks "is it raw" before "is this
#        combination legal".
# 11.10  Vitreo MATCHES (since 2026-09-28): GetData on an occlusion predicate
#        after an empty frame reports FALSE -- the count now comes from Metal
#        visibility results instead of a conservative TRUE -- and
#        CreatePredicate(SO_OVERFLOW_PREDICATE) succeeds, answering from the
#        stream-output stage's exact counts. Full query contract:
#        d3d11_a10_queries_probe and
#        .docs/audits/2026-09-28-d3d11-contract-audit/area-10-queries.md.
# dxgi.5 EnumAdapterByLuid matches exactly, both the hit and the miss code.
#        GetCreationFlags reports 0x80000000, an undocumented internal bit;
#        Vitreo reports 0, which is correct for the documented flag space.
#        CheckFeatureSupport on an unknown feature is DXGI_ERROR_INVALID_CALL
#        (0x887a0001) here, not DXGI_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED -- Vitreo was wrong.
#        EnumWarpAdapter succeeds here and ALLOW_TEARING reports TRUE even on
#        the basic render driver; both are deliberate Vitreo divergences (no
#        software rasterizer, and a presenter that is always vblank-synced).
#        EnumAdapterByGpuPreference(1) succeeds here because this machine has
#        more than one adapter, so the single-adapter case is not adjudicable.
